<title>UK: Daily Mail launches Oct 2004 stg exchangeable bond.</title>
<headline>Daily Mail launches Oct 2004 stg exchangeable bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following exchangeable bond was announced by lead manager J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DAILY MAIL AND GENERAL TRUST PLC</p>
<p> AMT    **		COUPON     2.50	MATURITY   *05.OCT.04</p>
<p> TYPE   EXCHANGEABLE  ISS PRICE  78.2-80.8 PAY DATE    =</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.5	 IND PREM   14-18 PCT YIELD	 5.75-6.25</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE DETERMINED. THE BOND WILL SERVE TO REFINANCE</p>
<p>		THE 47.9 MLN STG OUTSTANDING OF THE 5.75 PCT</p>
<p>		EXCHANGEABLE BONDS DUE 2003.</p>
<p>		THE BOND WILL BE EXCHANGABLE INTO SHARES OF</p>
<p>		REUTERS HOLDINGS PLC</p>
<p>	     *CALLABLE AT ACCRETED YIELD TO MATURITY FROM</p>
<p>		18.OCT.02</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
